<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Henry II the Pious</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1196–<a href="/years/1241">1241</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Henry II of Silesia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Henry II the Pious was Duke of Silesia and high duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> from 1238, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-bearded">Henry the Bearded</a> and Saint Hedwig. Like his father he sought to reunite the divided Polish duchies. He was killed fighting the Mongol invasion at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-legnica">Battle of Legnica</a> in April 1241, after which Silesia was divided among his sons.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henry-ii-the-pious.jpg" alt="Henry II the Pious" width="303" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Henryk_II_Pobo%C5%BCny_(Hedwig_Codex).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
